Local patch on the pinned upstream role grafana.grafana.grafana 6.1.0 (GPL-3.0-or-later).

Why: roles/grafana/tasks/dashboards.yml "Create dashboard folders" applies the
string filter regex_replace to a LIST (map(attribute='path') | sort). Ansible
coerces the list to a string, so the loop fails with "The `loop` value must
resolve to a 'list', not 'str'" whenever grafana_dashboards_dir is set (even for
a flat dashboard directory with no subdirectories). The fix maps the filter over
each item and forces a list.

Apply after installing the collection beside the brick (collections are
gitignored, so this patch must be re-applied on a fresh install):
  cd plugins/grafana/collections/ansible_collections/grafana/grafana
  patch -p1 < ../../../../patches/dashboards-loop-map.patch

roles.lock.json sha256 is aligned with the PATCHED role content.

--- a/roles/grafana/tasks/dashboards.yml
+++ b/roles/grafana/tasks/dashboards.yml
@@ -189,7 +189,7 @@
             owner: "grafana"
             group: "grafana"
             mode: "0755"
-          loop: "{{ __dashboards_subdirs.files | map(attribute='path') | sort | regex_replace(grafana_dashboards_dir + '/*', '') }}"
+          loop: "{{ __dashboards_subdirs.files | map(attribute='path') | sort | map('regex_replace', grafana_dashboards_dir + '/*', '') | list }}"
           become: true
           register: __dashboards_dir_created
           when: not ansible_check_mode
